name{cos}⁡(bt)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt))(p+q\\text{i}) \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+\\text{i}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\text{x}(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+{c}_{2}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q),\n$$\n\nwhere the parts $(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)$ and $(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q)$ are bounded.\n\nNow notice that the given curve is $\\text{unbounded},$ representing $\\text{a spiral}$ that is traversed $\\text{counterclockwise}.$ Thus, we must have $a\\ne 0.$\n\nAlso, notice that the spiral is traversed toward $\\text{the origin}.$\n\nHence, to insure that ${e}^{at}\\to 0,$ we require $a<0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523248 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186524053 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523248 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186524083 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523248 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186524084 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523248 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523248 #edb/ref 1045 "Phase Portraits for Linear Systems With Complex Eigenvalues" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523248 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186524083 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523248 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046644 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523248 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049209 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523248 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "f52aa899-b1e0-52c3-865d-5560a2dc7dfa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523310 #edb/ref 1080 "an ellipse" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523310 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523310 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1bd91dd1-c90f-56c1-8a22-a4fb47fa5f76" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523367 #edb/ref 1080 "clockwise" #edb/ref 17592186045417] 